Error [jet.UnknownFlag]: `--env-profile` isn't a flag `env` understands.
 Why: Jet ignores no flags silently, so a typo cannot quietly change a command.
 Fix: `env` takes `-p <pkg>...`, `--flake`, `--pure`, `--prep`, `--explain`, `--env <name>`, `--preset <name>`, `--trust`, `--local-nix-catalog <dir>`, `--shell-on-fail`, `--color=<when>`, `--no-color`, `--json`, `--offline`, `--fixtures <dir>`, `-y`, `--yes`.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2102